	(text "SNVSB49D table 10-3 (5 V, 400 kHz): 10 uH, 2 x 22 uF, 100k / 24.9k -> 5.02 V. EN tied to VIN.\n5 V: UCC12050 (HV-side sensor), AMC3330, PELV op amps / comparator / reference; 3.3 V: receivers,\nlogic, ISO7720F side 2, UCC21710 VCC, bias ENA."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 300.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0604c9d8-381c-58a2-8968-2e43b08e9a06")
	)
	(text "Trips at 19.70-20.44 V falling (20.16-20.64 V rising, 100k/2.00k 0.1 %): above the UCC14241 UVLO\n(17.1-18.9 V falling) and below the 21.6 V system minimum, so a vanishing +24V_GD turns every gate off\nactively (PWM gating + EN, latched) while the gate bias is still regulated. tpd(HL) 18 us."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 406.372 161.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "51a7c4eb-92b3-519b-840f-4d4b8df7aee2")
	)
	(text "interfaces.CELL. PWM1/2 = leg A high/low, PWM3/4 = leg B high/low. PWM5-8 and NTC_P/N not used (open).\nAN2_N / AN3_N = AGND (single-ended 0-3 V). +24V = +24V_GD from the CTRL eFuse (safety channel B):\nthis board draws <= 1.0 A and presents <= 600 uF to it (design_check)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 92.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "52052ba2-34e1-587c-b8ed-8cf9570369ce")
	)
	(text "FLT DRIVER, RDY (ACTIVE HIGH), DRIVER FAULT / READY LINES"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 398.844 19 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5afb0a05-5cb6-5265-a7e8-98e2369f6c70")
	)
	(text "Each pair: P 470R to GND, N 470R to 3.3 V, 120R across (= termination). AM26LV32E: VID <= -0.2 V -> output LOW.\nCable unplugged / pair open: VID <= -0.303 V worst case (3.135 V, 1 %, ri 4 k) -> LOW = gate off.\nCTRL unpowered: its AM26LV31E outputs are high-Z (IO(OFF) <= 100 uA) -> VID <= -0.293 V -> LOW = off.\nThis board's 3.3 V absent: receivers, gates and UCC21710 VCC dead, UCC14241 ENA low -> no gate bias;\nPWM/EN nets held low by 10 k. With the whole CELL cable out this board has no +24V at all."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 122.056 106.46 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6fd33d8b-1dce-5e67-8ca0-294ef6736056")
	)
	(text "LOCAL 5 V (LMR36015) AND 3.3 V (TPS7A2033) FROM THE CELL +24V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 225.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7e10c41c-7245-501a-a449-049bd8885397")
	)
	(text "TRIP_N = OC_H & OC_L & DC_H & DC_L & OV_OK & UV_OK -> LVC1G74 PRE: LATCH_OK low until the CTRL takes EN low\n(CLR). LR_OK = LATCH_OK & RDY_L. EN_DRV = EN_RX & LR_OK -> RST/EN of the 4 drivers (<= 0.8 us filter, clears\nDESAT latches). RUN = EN_DRV & DRV_FLT_N gates every PWM (fast path ~0.25 us): a trip, a driver UVLO, a\n+24V dip or a DESAT anywhere turns the whole bridge off. FLT_OK = LR_OK & DRV_FLT_N & TRIP_N: DESAT, driver\nUVLO, local OC / DC-flux / OV / +24V UV; TRIP_N direct, so a standing trip shows while EN is low (PRE = CLR = L\ngives Q_N = H). RDY_DRV = RDY_L & UV_OK. Gates: U_a OC/DC/I/IV, U_b TRIP/LR/EN/RUN, U_c FLT/RDY + 1 spare."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 213.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "92ec554d-ec90-5ced-9dfc-bb563c2b0d0d")
	)
	(text "TRIP LATCH, ENABLES, FLT (NO FIRMWARE IN THE PATH; INT-17, INT-18)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 118.96 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
